# Using the World-Wide Web to Deliver Complex Electronic Documents: Implications for Libraries.

**Authors:** Price-Wilkin, John

## Abstract
Explores the benefits and limitations of the World Wide Web in the context of projects taking place at the University of Virginia Library and the university's Institute for Advanced Technology in the Humanities. A gateway between the Web and PAT, a text retrieval program based on SGML (Standard Generalized Markup Language), is described. (Contains four references.) (Author/KRN)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ486773

